<title>SINGAPORE: Taiwan sells two Oct diesel cargoes below $27/bbl.</title>
<headline>Taiwan sells two Oct diesel cargoes below $27/bbl.</headline>
<text>
<p>SINGAPORE, Sept 18 (Reuter) Taiwan's state-owned Chinese Petroleum Corp (CPC) sold by tender two 225,000-250,000-barrel cargoes of 0.3 percent sulphur diesel at slightly below $27.00 per barrel on a free-on-board (fob) basis, a CPC source said on Wednesday.</p>
<p>The cargoes were for lifting during October 1-23 from Kaoshiung.</p>
<p>In its last tender, CPC sold one 225,000-250,000-barrel of diesel at $25.50-25.55 per barrel fob Kaoshiung.</p>
<p>--Singapore Newsroom (+65-870-3093)</p>
</text>
